{
  "name": "How to Improve Your Business's AI \"Trust Score\"",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Want AI to recommend your business more often?",
      "text": "Want AI to recommend your business more often? It's all about building a strong \"trust score\" by making your business a clear, trusted entity online. AI systems are designed to recommend the most relevant and reliable information, and they do this by piecing together a picture of your business from countless sources. If that picture is messy or inconsistent, AI will likely skip over you. Entity optimization is the key here—it's about ensuring all the facts about your business, like your name, address, contact info, and services, are consistent and clearly presented everywhere online, not just on your website. This consistency signals trustworthiness to AI and helps it understand exactly who you are and what you offer.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Start by creating a canonical, structured list of all your services…",
      "text": "Start by creating a canonical, structured list of all your services, exactly as your clients would search for them. Don't just list broad categories; break them down into specific offerings. For example, instead of 'Plumbing Services,' detail 'Emergency Leak Repair,' 'Water Heater Installation,' and 'Drain Cleaning.' This specificity helps AI match your services to precise user queries. Next, clearly define your service areas. List every city and region you serve so AI can accurately recommend you for local searches. Ensure these details are consistent across your website, Google Business Profile, and any other online directories. Finally, make sure information about your team members is available and consistent, as this adds another layer of legitimacy. Regularly audit your online presence for any discrepancies and correct them promptly to keep that trust score high. If your business is complex with multiple locations or brands, this process can get tricky.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
